{title: A Hymn of Glory Let Us Sing}
{artist: The Venerable Bede · tr. Benjamin Webb & Elizabeth Rundle Charles}
{key: D}
{time: 6/4}
{tempo: 160}

Verse 1
[D]A hymn [Em7]of glory [D]let us sing! [Bm]New hymns [Em7]throughout the [A]world shall [A7]ring:
Alleluia! [D]Alleluia! Christ by [G]a way [D]none ever [Bm]trod,
Ascends [Em7]unto the [A]throne of God. [A7]Alleluia!

Verse 2
The [D]angels say [G]to the [D]elev'n, "Why [Bm]stand ye gazing [A]into heav'n?"
[Bm7]Alleluia! Alleluia! [E]This is [A]the Savior [D]This is He!
[Em7]Jesus has [D]triumphed gloriously. [Bm7]Alleluia!

Verse 3
Again [A7]shall ye [D]behold Him so [G]As ye [A]today have [A7]seen Him [D]go;
Alleluia! [A7]Alleluia! Calm soaring [D]through the [G]radiant sky,
[D]Mounting its [A]dazzling summits [D]high. Alleluia!

Verse 4
May [A]our affections [G]there do [Bm7]tend, And [Em7]with unwearied [A7]hearts ascend,
Alleluia! [D]Alleluia! Toward [Em7]Thy kingdom's [D]throne where [Em7]Thou
As [A7]in our faith [Bm]are seated [A]now. Alleluia!

Verse 5
[Bm7]Be Thou [E]our present [A]joy O Lord! [Bm7]Who will [F#m]be ever [Bm7]our reward,
[Em]Alleluia! Alleluia! [A7]And, as the [B7]countless ages [Em]flee,
May [D]all our [Em7]glory be [A]in Thee! Alleluia!

Chorus
[A7]Alleluia! Alleluia! [D]Alleluia! Alleluia!
